  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 Agreement to secure appropriate rent levels in accordance with the Local Housing Allowance, the development would fail to secure the proposed House in Multiple Occupation at an affordable rent level, contrary to policy LP22 (&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-367e19e0-7fff-344c-6cf4-0c8949579d87&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;Houses in Multiple Occupation (HMO)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 Agreement securing appropriate mitigation by restricting future occupiers of the development from obtaining parking permits within the Controlled Parking Zone, the proposed development would likely exacerbate existing parking stress and congestion on the surrounding highway network. The development would, therefore, be contrary to policy LP45 (&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;Parking and Car-Free Development) of&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020) and policy T6 (Car parking) of the London Plan (2021).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-e057688f-7fff-196c-6173-8da6ba09c77e&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Insufficient information has been provided to demonstrate that the occupiers of bedrooms 1 and 2 at the basement level would receive sufficient light, outlook, and ventilation. The proposal, therefore, results in a substandard form of accommodation contrary to policies LP17 (Housing Design) and LP22 (&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;Houses in Multiple Occupation (HMO)) &lt;/span&gt;of the&amp;nbsp;Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and policy D6 (Housing quality and standards) of the London Plan (2021).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-d6c9bc68-7fff-714e-95c3-c6b90496f3b1&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of unacceptable cycle parking provision, fails to provide secure, accessible, convenient, and weatherproof cycle parking storage that includes an adequate level of parking suitable for accessible bicycles, tricycles, and cargo bikes required by policy LP42 of the Hackney Local Plan (2020).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
